course: dictionary
lesson: 7784
title: A word from another language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from other languages, and you may meet one in any book. «Qi Baishi was a famous 20th-century Chinese painter.» Qi is the name of a person here, and the sentence tells you what he painted, so you can learn more about the name from the words around it.
explain: The word qi is from Mandarin, a language spoken in China. In Chinese thought and traditional medicine, qi is a life energy believed to flow through the body. The word is said like «chee» to an English ear.
explain: Context helps you work out a word's meaning. «Tai chi» is a practice of breathing and slow movements, and people try to balance their qi. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Qi (Mandarin, pinyin: qi) is a noun. Pinyin is a way of writing Chinese sounds using the letters of the English alphabet.
fact: «Qi» means life energy in Chinese thought and traditional medicine, and it is said like «chee».
fact: In everyday Mandarin, qì means air, gas, breath or spirit, while other syllables spelled «qi» mean seven, to ride and to rise.
fact: «Qi» is a famous word that is allowed in Scrabble.
fact: «Qi Baishi» was a famous 20th-century Chinese painter who painted shrimps, crabs, birds and flowers with simple ink.
exercise: In Chinese thought and traditional medicine, what is qi? | A number between six and eight | A famous painter from the 1900s | A kind of noodle eaten in Beijing | *A life energy believed to flow through the body and all living things
exercise: «Qi Baishi was a famous 20th-century Chinese painter of simple ink paintings of shrimps.» What did Qi Baishi paint? | Faces broken into shapes | Castles on a hill | Cars, trains and planes | *Shrimps, crabs, birds and flowers
exercise: «Tai chi helps people practise breathing and slow movements to balance their qi.» What do people try to balance in tai chi? | *Their qi | Their painting strokes | The weather | Their shoes
test: Scientists have not found qi as a measurable energy. What does this tell you about qi? | It is a type of ink | It is a machine | It is proven by every scientist | *It is part of a tradition and belief, not something measured
test: The spelling «qi» can mean seven in Mandarin, so what does this show? | Qi only means air | *Some words spelled qi have different meanings | Qi always means seven | Qi is the name of a city
exam: Why is it helpful to read the words around a new word like qi? | Only the first word of a sentence matters | The words around it are always wrong | You must never read on | *Context clues can help you work out what the word means
